            <div class="eyebrow">SAP CPI CASE STUDY</div>

            <h1>Contract & Agreement Automation</h1>

            <p>
                Complex SAP CPI integration between SAP SuccessFactors,
                Azure Service Bus and Icertis to automate the creation,
                processing and lifecycle management of multiple employee
                agreements and contractual addendums.
            </p>

            <div class="project-tags">
                <span>SAP CPI</span>
                <span>SAP SuccessFactors</span>
                <span>Azure Service Bus</span>
                <span>Icertis</span>
                <span>OpenText</span>
                <span>REST APIs</span>
                <span>OData</span>
                <span>Data Store</span>
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OVERVIEW -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">01. Overview</div>

            <h2>Project Overview</h2>

            <p>
                This project involved the development of a complex SAP CPI
                integration between SAP SuccessFactors, Azure Service Bus
                and Icertis to automate employee agreement and contractual
                addendum processes.
            </p>

            <p>
                The solution supports more than 10 different agreement and
                addendum types, each with its own business rules, data
                requirements, document structure and variables.
            </p>

            <p>
                SAP CPI acts as the central orchestration layer, coordinating
                SuccessFactors employee and workflow data, asynchronous
                messages from Azure Service Bus and agreement processing
                in Icertis.
            </p>

        </section>


        <!-- ARCHITECTURE -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">02. Architecture</div>

            <h2>Integration Architecture</h2>

            <p>
                The solution connects SAP SuccessFactors, SAP CPI,
                Azure Service Bus, Icertis and OpenText across different
                stages of the agreement lifecycle.
            </p>

            <div class="architecture-flow">

                <div class="architecture-box">
                    SAP SuccessFactors
                    <small>Employee Data · Workflow</small>
                </div>

                <div class="architecture-arrow">↓</div>

                <div class="architecture-box">
                    SAP CPI
                    <small>Orchestration · Validation · Mapping · Business Logic</small>
                </div>

                <div class="architecture-arrow">↓</div>

                <div class="architecture-box">
                    Icertis
                    <small>Agreement Creation & Management</small>
                </div>

                <div class="architecture-arrow">↓</div>

                <div class="architecture-box">
                    Azure Service Bus
                    <small>Asynchronous Agreement Status Messages</small>
                </div>

                <div class="architecture-arrow">↓</div>

                <div class="architecture-box">
                    SAP SuccessFactors / OpenText
                    <small>Workflow & Document Processing</small>
                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- AGREEMENT TYPES -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">03. Agreement Automation</div>

            <h2>Multiple Agreement & Addendum Types</h2>

            <p>
                One of the main challenges of the integration was supporting
                more than 10 different agreement and contractual addendum types
                within the same integration landscape.
            </p>

            <p>
                Each agreement type has its own business rules, structures,
                required variables and data requirements.
            </p>

            <p>
                SAP CPI applies the appropriate processing logic based on the
                agreement type and prepares the corresponding data required
                for agreement creation in Icertis.
            </p>

        </section>


        <!-- FLOW 1 -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">04. Agreement Initialization</div>

            <h2>SuccessFactors → CPI → Icertis</h2>

            <p>
                The first integration flow periodically processes eligible
                SuccessFactors workflows and retrieves the employee, job
                and workflow information required for agreement creation.
            </p>

            <p>
                SAP CPI orchestrates the required SuccessFactors OData calls,
                applies the business logic associated with the corresponding
                agreement type and builds the agreement initialization payload.
            </p>

            <p>
                The request is then sent to Icertis to create the agreement.
                Once created, the agreement identifier returned by Icertis
                is associated with the corresponding SuccessFactors process
                so that the agreement can be tracked throughout its lifecycle.
            </p>

            <div class="process-line">
                SuccessFactors → SAP CPI → Retrieve Employee Data → Apply Agreement Logic → Create Agreement → Icertis
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- AZURE SERVICE BUS -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">05. Asynchronous Processing</div>

            <h2>Azure Service Bus Integration</h2>

            <p>
                Azure Service Bus Queues are used to support asynchronous
                communication between the agreement process and SAP CPI.
            </p>

            <p>
                SAP CPI consumes messages from Azure Service Bus to determine
                the outcome of an agreement and trigger the corresponding
                downstream processing.
            </p>

            <p>
                Depending on the received status, SAP CPI determines whether
                the related SuccessFactors workflow should be canceled or
                allowed to continue to its next step.
            </p>

        </section>


        <!-- FLOW 2 -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">06. Agreement Execution</div>

            <h2>Azure Service Bus → CPI → SuccessFactors</h2>

            <p>
                The second integration flow is triggered by messages received
                through Azure Service Bus.
            </p>

            <p>
                These messages provide SAP CPI with the agreement processing
                result and determine how the corresponding SuccessFactors
                workflow should continue.
            </p>

            <div class="challenge-grid">

                <article>
                    <h3>Agreement Canceled</h3>

                    <p>
                        When a cancellation status is received, SAP CPI applies
                        the corresponding processing logic and updates the
                        related SuccessFactors process accordingly.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>Agreement Approved</h3>

                    <p>
                        When the agreement is approved or executed, SAP CPI
                        processes the finalized agreement information and
                        allows the corresponding SuccessFactors workflow
                        to continue to its next step.
                    </p>
                </article>

            </div>

            <div class="process-line">
                Azure Service Bus → SAP CPI → Evaluate Status → Cancel Process / Continue Workflow
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- DOCUMENT PROCESSING -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">07. Document Processing</div>

            <h2>Agreement Document Handling</h2>

            <p>
                As part of the agreement completion process, SAP CPI retrieves
                and processes the finalized agreement document.
            </p>

            <p>
                The document is stored in SAP SuccessFactors Employee Central
                together with the required agreement information.
            </p>

            <p>
                From SuccessFactors, the document is transferred to OpenText
                through the existing standard document integration.
            </p>

        </section>


        <!-- QUARANTINE -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">08. Error Handling</div>

            <h2>Configurable Quarantine Strategy</h2>

            <p>
                A key challenge was controlling repeated processing failures.
            </p>

            <p>
                Because eligible SuccessFactors workflows are checked
                periodically, a workflow experiencing an error could otherwise
                be selected and processed again on every integration execution.
                This could generate repeated failures and unnecessary
                error notifications.
            </p>

            <p>
                To address this, I implemented a configurable quarantine
                mechanism using SAP CPI Data Store.
            </p>

            <p>
                When a transaction fails, it is placed in quarantine and
                temporarily excluded from normal processing. The transaction
                becomes eligible for processing again only after the configured
                quarantine period.
            </p>

            <p>
                The current quarantine period is 24 hours, but the duration
                can be adjusted without modifying the integration flow.
            </p>

        </section>


        <!-- WHY QUARANTINE -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">09. Operational Resilience</div>

            <h2>Reducing Repeated Errors</h2>

            <div class="challenge-grid">

                <article>
                    <h3>Without Quarantine</h3>

                    <p>
                        A failed workflow could be selected again during every
                        scheduled integration run, causing the same error to
                        be processed repeatedly and generating unnecessary
                        notifications.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>With Quarantine</h3>

                    <p>
                        Failed transactions are temporarily persisted and
                        excluded from normal processing, allowing time for
                        the underlying issue to be resolved before another
                        processing attempt.
                    </p>
                </article>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- TECHNICAL FEATURES -->
        <section class="section">

            <div class="eyebrow">10. Technical Highlights</div>

            <h2>Key Technical Features</h2>

            <div class="value-grid">

                <article>
                    <h3>Multi-Agreement Processing</h3>

                    <p>
                        Support for more than 10 agreement and addendum types
                        with different business rules, data structures and
                        required variables.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>Azure Service Bus Integration</h3>

                    <p>
                        Asynchronous processing of agreement status messages
                        and downstream actions using Azure Service Bus Queues.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>OData Orchestration</h3>

                    <p>
                        Retrieval and consolidation of employee, job and
                        workflow information from SAP SuccessFactors.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>Dynamic Business Logic</h3>

                    <p>
                        Agreement-specific processing according to the
                        requirements of each contractual document type.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>Configurable Quarantine</h3>

                    <p>
                        Data Store-based mechanism used to temporarily isolate
                        failed transactions before allowing reprocessing.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>Error Notification Optimization</h3>

                    <p>
                        Prevention of repeated error notifications caused by
                        continuously reprocessing the same unresolved workflow.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>Document Handling</h3>

                    <p>
                        Processing of finalized agreement documents for storage
                        in SAP SuccessFactors and downstream transfer to OpenText.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <h3>Workflow Integration</h3>

                    <p>
                        Coordination of agreement status with SuccessFactors
                        workflow continuation and cancellation logic.
                    </p>
                </article>

            </div>

        </section>


